@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 0. Create admin (once; 409 = already exists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Test Admin", "email": "admin@test.com", "password": "Passw0rd!", "role": "admin" }

### 1. Admin login (captures token for later tests)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@test.com", "password": "Passw0rd!" }

### 2. Driver login (driver account was made via /driver/register page)
# @name driverLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "driver@test.com", "password": "Passw0rd!" }

### 3. No token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/driver/license/whatever.jpg

### 4. Garbage token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/driver/license/whatever.jpg
Authorization: Bearer garbage

### 5. Driver token -> 403  (THE T3 TEST)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/driver/license/whatever.jpg
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.token}}

### 6. Admin + missing file -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/driver/license/whatever.jpg
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

### 7. Admin + path traversal -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/driver/license/..%2Fsecret
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

### 8. Driver + path traversal -> 403 (role gate runs before path check)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/driver/license/..%2Fsecret
Authorization: Bearer {{driverLogin.response.body.token}}

### 9. Admin + REAL file -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/driver/license//5-62b19987ece86639.pdf
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

### 10. Admin via ?token= param -> 200 (regression: admin page link)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/driver/license//5-62b19987ece86639.pdf?token={{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

### 11. Driver via ?token= param -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/driver/license//5-62b19987ece86639.pdf?token={{driverLogin.response.body.token}}
